🧱 1. What is a Stack?

A stack is a linear data structure that follows LIFO (Last In, First Out).   
👉 The element added last is the one removed first.   

Common operations:

Operation	             Description

push(x)	                Add element x on top of the stack
pop()	                Remove the top element
peek() or top()	        See the top element without removing it
isEmpty()	            Check if stack is empty

# create empty stack

stack = []

# push(x) → add element on top

stack.append(10)
stack.append(20)
stack.append(30)

# pop() → remove top element
stack.pop()

# peek() / top() → see top element
top_element = stack[-1]
print(top_element)

# isEmpty() → check stack is empty or not
if len(stack) == 0:
    print("Stack is empty")
else:
    print("Stack is not empty")


